WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:02.965
Now let's use the numbers.

00:00:03.315 --> 00:00:07.981
Why average? One trial can be a little off, and an average evens that out.

00:00:08.631 --> 00:00:15.020
Say three trials gave diameters of 10, 9.5, and 10.5 centimeters.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.837
Add the three trials. That makes 30.

00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:24.266
Then divide by 3. The average diameter is 10 centimeters.

00:00:25.716 --> 00:00:29.696
Next, use Figure 1 to turn that diameter into a lung volume.

00:00:30.146 --> 00:00:34.440
Figure 1 matches a balloon's diameter to the volume of air inside.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.846
Find 10 centimeters on the bottom axis.

00:00:38.896 --> 00:00:41.469
Trace straight up, until you reach the curve.

00:00:42.919 --> 00:00:45.692
Then trace straight across, to the volume axis.

00:00:47.142 --> 00:00:50.954
Read the lung volume: about 520 milliliters.

00:00:52.204 --> 00:00:55.076
Do the same thing for each diameter you measure.
